       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg/day, and a single 1600 mg dose is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), a common regimen for mild to moderate pain\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it now."
