       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. I'm not aware of any indication where that dose is safe or more effective. Above about 3,200 mg/day, ibuprofen gives no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and the risks of GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular events keep rising. I'm not willing to put in an order that could seriously harm the patient, and this one isn't something I can enter on authority alone.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum labeled dose.\n- Enter a lower regimen, such as **400 mg or 600 mg PO four times daily**.\n- Enter a different agent or add an adjunct, if the goal is stronger analgesia.\n\nIf you have a specific protocol or trial that calls for this dose, it should go through your pharmacy and the formal override or exception process. Pharmacy can review and verify it independently. I can also help draft the details for that request.\n\nTell me which of the options above you'd like, and I'll enter it."
